damaged_code:
```
// Manual, dynamic string parsing to evaluate user role access
struct User {
    roles: Vec<String>,
}

fn check_permission(user: &User, required_scope: &str) -> bool {
    // Ad-hoc, untyped check prone to typos: "admin" vs "Admin"
    user.roles.iter().any(|role| {
        let formatted = format!("scope:{}", role);
        formatted == required_scope
    })
}
```

fix:
Model access scopes using strongly typed, compiled Enums.

```
// Safe compile-time checked scopes
#[derive(PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum Permission {
    ReadAuditLog,
    WriteMetrics,
}

pub struct User {
    pub permissions: Vec<Permission>,
}

fn authorize(user: &User, required: Permission) -> bool {
    user.permissions.contains(&required)
}
```
